<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Where is each point? Choose from the list.</p><div><m>({0},\,{0},\,{6})</m>: [ on the x-axis | on the y-axis | on the z-axis | in the xy-plane, not on an axis | in the yz-plane, not on an axis | in the xz-plane, not on an axis | in no coordinate plane ]  </div><div><m>({5},\,{2},\,{-4})</m>: [ on the x-axis | on the y-axis | on the z-axis | in the xy-plane, not on an axis | in the yz-plane, not on an axis | in the xz-plane, not on an axis | in no coordinate plane ]  </div><div><m>({0},\,{7},\,{0})</m>: [ on the x-axis | on the y-axis | on the z-axis | in the xy-plane, not on an axis | in the yz-plane, not on an axis | in the xz-plane, not on an axis | in no coordinate plane ]  </div><div><m>({-2},\,{0},\,{7})</m>: [ on the x-axis | on the y-axis | on the z-axis | in the xy-plane, not on an axis | in the yz-plane, not on an axis | in the xz-plane, not on an axis | in no coordinate plane ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Count the zero coordinates. One zero puts a point in a coordinate plane: z = 0 is the xy-plane, x = 0 the yz-plane and y = 0 the xz-plane. Two zeros put it on an axis, where two planes meet.</p><ul><li><m>({0},\,{0},\,{6})</m>: on the z-axis.</li><li><m>({5},\,{2},\,{-4})</m>: in no coordinate plane.</li><li><m>({0},\,{7},\,{0})</m>: on the y-axis.</li><li><m>({-2},\,{0},\,{7})</m>: in the xz-plane, not on an axis.</li></ul></p></solution>
    <answer><p>on the z-axis</p></answer>
    <answer><p>in no coordinate plane</p></answer>
    <answer><p>on the y-axis</p></answer>
    <answer><p>in the xz-plane, not on an axis</p></answer>
</stack-static>